sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS 4 + R1-R4 (process.stop shape: 209, @swamp/ssh, full intent as inputs).
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 1-22 (cfgmgmt absent applies, mirror of process:create, no shipped scripts, no report step).
  %% Rule 23: 2026-11-03 required-only main path.
  %% status: migrated
  %% command: process:destroy
  %% kind: process.destroy
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: process:destroy 417
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit process:destroy 417`
  %%> - syntax: `process:destroy <process> [--project=ID] [--yes] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the numeric Process ID; the CLI asks for confirmation first
  %%> Optional:
  %%> - `--yes` skips the confirmation; `--idempotency-key` reuses a task start; `--json` returns JSON; none adds a step
  %%> Not handled here:
  %%> - `--project` removes a Project definition only; it starts no run (R1)
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Check Process dependencies
  alt attached Node service
    GW--xCLI: Process required (409)<br/>No admission or runtime change
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - process.required_by_instance_node_service names every dependent Instance before recording an Operation; the Process, runtime and attachments remain.
  else no attachment dependency
  Note over GW: Validate, record the task<br/>Process 417: removing · #5130
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the Process's Node
  %%> - no Route points to the Process, else `process.has_routes`
  %%> - the Process is not required by a Database server
  %%> Result:
  %%> - Process 417 marked removing; the record stays until the run succeeds
  %%> - task #5130 recorded with the full intent
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-process-destroy
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209); every step runs there
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - `kind`: process.destroy
  %%> - the unit or container name and runtime, and for Vite the Instance environment path
  %%> - the Node's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  %%> Checked by the input schema:
  %%> - no step reads or re-checks the intent
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5130
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  alt systemd
    SW->>N: Disable and stop the unit<br/>cfgmgmt/systemd.apply
    SW->>N: Stop the unit<br/>ssh exec · stop
    SW->>N: Remove the unit<br/>cfgmgmt/file absent
    SW->>N: Reload systemd<br/>ssh exec · daemon-reload
    SW->>N: Check unit removal<br/>cfgmgmt/file.check
    SW->>N: Check boot removal<br/>cfgmgmt/file.check
    SW->>N: Read removed unit state<br/>ssh exec · systemctl show
    SW->>N: Clear failed unit cache<br/>ssh exec · reset-failed
    %%> Only the admitted unit is reset, after its file and boot link are absent, LoadState is not-found, and no PID, cgroup or pending job remains.
    %%> A failed state alone never permits cleanup. Other remaining runtime or boot state fails the end check.
    SW->>N: Check the unit<br/>ssh exec · systemctl show
    %%> Reads the state again after cache cleanup; a running or loaded unit, boot policy, PID, cgroup or pending job refuses completion.
  else Docker
    SW->>N: Remove the container<br/>cfgmgmt/docker_container
    SW->>N: Check container removal<br/>cfgmgmt/docker_container
  end
  SW->>N: Remove the environment<br/>cfgmgmt/directory absent
  opt Vite dev Process
    SW->>N: Remove the dev environment<br/>cfgmgmt/file absent
  end
  SW->>N: Verify it is gone<br/>native assert
  %%> Asserts absent unit/container and runtime and boot state; data volumes and the source environment file remain.
  alt all removed
    N-->>SW: unit gone
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - nothing of Process 417 is left on the Node
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event and reads the end check's output; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Delete the record<br/>Process 417 removed
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the Process record is deleted
    %%> - task #5130 succeeds
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0
    %%> When:
    %%> - SSH fails, or something of Process 417 is still there after the removal
    %%> How:
    %%> - the failing step ends the run with its own exit code; there is no report step
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its exit code, mapped to `error_code`
    Note over GW: Keep the record, failed<br/>task failed · repeat destroy
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Process 417 keeps its record, marked with the error code
    %%> - repeat `process:destroy` to converge
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5130
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
  end
